            <h2>Route Overview: Charlotte to Raleigh</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Charlotte to Raleigh by train is one of the most efficient and popular ways to connect North Carolina's two largest cities, linking the Queen City with the state capital. This route is primarily served by the Piedmont and Carolinian services, making it a preferred choice for both business commuters and leisure travelers exploring the Research Triangle region.</p>
            <p>This route is especially popular because it combines reliable rail service with frequent daily departures. The presence of state-supported train services means you can travel between these major cities quickly and affordably, making it a strong alternative to driving on I-85/I-40 or taking a flight.</p>
